You label ONE relationship for a knowledge graph.

SOURCE = source document.
TARGET = linked entity.
TEXT = short context around the TARGET.

The graph edge is:

SOURCE --predicate--> TARGET

Choose a specific predicate that makes this a TRUE natural statement
based only on the provided TEXT.

The predicate must be supported by the TEXT.
Do not invent, assume, or infer a relationship that is not supported
by the provided TEXT.

Return exactly:

1{TUPLE_DELIM}PREDICATE{TUPLE_DELIM}DESCRIPTION{TUPLE_DELIM}STRENGTH{RECORD_DELIM}

Rules:

PREDICATE:
- snake_case
- 2-5 words
- specific relationship
- NEVER use related_to, mentions, references, has_link

DESCRIPTION:
- one complete sentence
- maximum 25 words
- describe the relationship supported by the TEXT

STRENGTH:
- integer 1-10
- 10 = explicit/central in the TEXT
- 1 = passing or weak mention
- assign the strength only from evidence in the TEXT

No JSON.
No markdown.
No extra text.
"""
